So `commands.ssh(target)` produced no destination?! Let me look at SshCommandLine.ssh():

```java
public List<String> ssh(SshTarget target) {
    var command = new ArrayList<String>();
    command.add("ssh");
    command.addAll(connectionArguments(target, "-p"));
    ...
}
```

Does `ssh()` add the destination? Let me read the file. If `ssh()` doesn't append the destination, callers append it (RemoteHostInstaller appends the destination + remote command). My probe appended only "true" — so the message went to host "true".

Let me verify by reading SshCommandLine.
